{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792454798788,"sessionID":"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"websearch","callID":"call_00_a5G9gffOMlCs6QY0iC346543","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"query":"Laloy Vrugt 2012 DREAM \"50 million surrogate model evaluations\" Keating 241-parameter groundwater","numResults":6},"output":"{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_6feee4ea2952b4c8a21c993feb9e56ad\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1029/2011wr010608\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\\nby E Laloy · 2012 · Cited by 663 — Here we present our latest algorithmic developments and introduce MT-DREAM(ZS), which combines the strengths of multiple-try sampling, snooker\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011wr010608\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\\nby E Laloy · 2012 · Cited by 663 — In this paper, we present a general framework for efficient inversion of highly parameterized models. This method, entitled MT-DREAM(ZS),\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1532997\",\n      \"title\": \"Quantifying model structural error: Efficient Bayesian calibration of a regional groundwater flow model using surrogates and a data&#8208;driven error model\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2017-06-14\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"In this study, we use DREAM-ZS (DiffeRential Evolution Adaptive Metropolis algorithm), a Mar- kov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) sampler [Vrugt et al., 2009; Laloy and Vrugt, 2012; Vrugt, 2016] to estimate the distribution.\\n2.2. The Error-Explicit Bayesian Method: Predictive Uncertainty Once sufficient samples fhi; /ig; i51; . . .\\nWe do not add surrogate error because we will run the full SVRP model during the prediction phase.\\nThe DREAM-ZS runtime setting is configured following the recommendations in Vrugt et al. [2008].\\nWhen the surrogate accuracy is not satisfactory for Bayesian inference, a two-stage MCMC simulation scheme [Cui et al., 2011; Elsheikh et al., 2014; Laloy et al., 2013] can be used to prevent the sampling bias arising from using surrogate models. In the two-stage scheme, a surrogate model is first evaluated for every proposal generated by MCMC.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.semanticscholar.org/author/E.-Laloy/5346056\",\n      \"title\": \"E. Laloy | Semantic Scholar\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nE. Laloy J. Vrugt\\nEnvironmental Science, Computer Science\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\n* 1 January 2012\\nTLDR\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nMT‐DREAM(ZS), which combines the strengths of multiple‐try sampling, snooker updating, and sampling from an archive of past states is introduced, which is especially designed to solve high‐dimensional search problems and\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nreceives particularly spectacular performance improvement over other adaptive MCMC approaches when using distributed computing. Expand\\n* 538\\n* 30\\n* PDF (opens in a new tab)\\nWiley (opens in a new tab)\\nSave\\nAlert\\nCite\\nEfficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nE. Laloy B. Rogiers J. Vrugt D. Mallants D. Jacques\\nEnvironmental Science\\nEfficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\n* 1 May 2013\\nTLDR\\nParameter optimization and uncertainty analysis for plot-scale continuous modeling of runoff using a formal Bayesian approach.\\nE. Laloy D. Fasbender C. Bielders\\nEnvironmental Science, Engineering\\nParameter optimization and uncertainty analysis for plot-scale continuous modeling of runoff using a formal Bayesian approach.\\nThis study reports on the use the recently developed Differential Evolution Adaptative Metropolis algorithm (DREAM) to calibrate in a Bayesian framework the continuous, spatially distributed, … Expand\\n* 52\\n* 4\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/2417772\",\n      \"title\": \"Quantifying subsurface parameter and transport uncertainty using surrogate modelling and environmental tracers\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2022-11-01\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"original physics-based model (Asher et al., 2015; Razavi et al., 2012).\\nFor instance, Laloy and Jacques (2019) and Fienen et al. (2018) com-\\npare the ability of multiple surrogate models to emulate physics-based\\nreactive transport models at the column scale and groundwater flow\\nat regional scale, respectively. Recent studies extend the use of\\nthe high-fidelity model evaluated with parameter vector realisation mi are represented as d sim i .\\n2.4 | Neural network surrogate model\\nA single high-fidelity model run takes up to 10 min when distributed\\nover 144 computational cores. Scaling these runtimes to a full MCMC\\ncalibration that requires 100000's of model evaluations performed\\nAugmenting the observation error with the surrogate\\nmodelling validation error is a similar approach taken by (Xu\\net al., 2017). We use the computationally cheap trained surrogate\\nmodel to evaluate all likelihood function evaluations.\\nBayesian inference of model parameters is achieved by sampling\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://users.cms.caltech.edu/~venkatc/paclrst_cagroundwater_jgr24.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Modeling Groundwater Levels in California's Central Valley ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"system is challenging due to low‐quality well data which is sparsely and noisily sampled across time and space.\\nThe lack of consistent well data makes it difficult to evaluate the impact of 2017 and 2019 wet years on CV\\ngroundwater following a severe drought during 2012–2015. A novel machine learning method is formulated for\\nhan, 2020 ), unlike kriging‐based approaches. Stochastic search methods, such as Markov Chain Monte‐Carlo\\n(MCMC), are often necessitated for model inversion with uncertainty quantification (Hermans et al., 2015 ;\\nKeating et al., 2013 ; Laloy et al., 2013 ; Mariethoz et al., 2010 ). Stochastic search methods are known for their\\ncomputational complexity, especially when optimizing for 3D aquifer models with millions of grid cells.\\nGiven the several limitations associated with subsurface modeling, we adopt a data‐driven approach to\\ngroundwater modeling and uncertainty quantification. In many cases, the final groundwater management de-\\nNote that the simplifying assumption of 2D variability of water levels is made to facilitate initial evaluation of the\\nefficacy of GP‐DNN methodology for hydrological modeling. Extending proposed methodology for rigorous 3D‐\\nmodeling of groundwater levels, where vertical connectivities between all 13 aquifer model layers are accounted\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://bg.copernicus.org/preprints/bg-2017-41/bg-2017-41-SC2-supplement.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Microsoft Word - Reponse_SC1.docx\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"On the other hand, Laloy and Vrugt (2012) demonstrated that DREAM can successfully sample the 25-dimensional, three-modal Gaussian function with the two neighboring modes having a separation of 10 units.\\nLaloy, E., and J.A. Vrugt: High-dimensional posterior exploration of hudrologic models using multiply-try DREAM(zs) and high-performance computing, Water resour. Res., 48, W01526, 2012.\\nVrugt, J.A.: Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation using the DREAM software package: Theory, concepts, and MATLAB implementation, Environmental modeling & Software, 75, 273-316, 2016.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/preprints/gmd-2018-272/gmd-2018-272-AR3.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Bold black font: Topical editor and reviewer comments Black font: Author response Topical Editor Decision: Publish subject to technical corrections\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"the soil respiration model parameters using the MT-DREAM(ZS) code (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012). 319\\nMT-DREAM(ZS) implements a Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm by running 320\\nmultiple Markov chains in parallel with adaptive proposal distribution, multiple-try sampling, and 321\\nsampling from an archive of past states.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/sir20125062\",\n      \"title\": \"Groundwater simulation and management models for the upper Klamath Basin, Oregon and California\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2012-05-04\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Suggested Citation\\nGannett, M.W., Wagner, B.J., and Lite, K.E., 2012, Groundwater simulation and management models for the upper Klamath Basin, Oregon and California: U.S. Geological Survey Scientific Investigations Report 2012-5062, x, 92 p.; Figures; Tables; HTML Document, https://doi.org/10.3133/sir20125062.\\nISSN: 2328-0328 (online)\\n* Publication type | Report\\n* Publication Subtype | USGS Numbered Series\\n* Title | Groundwater simulation and management models for the upper Klamath Basin, Oregon and California\\n* Series title | Scientific Investigations Report\\n* Series number | 2012-5062\\n* DOI | 10.3133/sir20125062\\n* Year Published | 2012\\n* Language | English\\n* Publisher | U.S.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M\"\n}","metadata":{"provider":"parallel","truncated":false},"title":"Parallel Web Search: Laloy Vrugt 2012 DREAM \"50 million surrogate model evaluations\" Keating 241-parameter groundwater","time":{"start":1792454798143,"end":1792454798783}},"id":"prt_156a1aa10001IPEvnnFp7a9IM2","sessionID":"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M","messageID":"msg_156a10342001f3u0wWJDkdq5gF"}}
