{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792454992321,"sessionID":"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"websearch","callID":"call_00_PTlEA1Lq0iJOWdtHOBCf1711","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"numResults":5,"query":"Laloy Vrugt 2012 W01526 \"50 million\" surrogate evaluations Keating 2010 \"241\" groundwater introduction"},"output":"{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_8fc454dd85377d04497f46948b19fc84\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://pubs.usgs.gov/ds/0997/ds997.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Groundwater-Quality Data from the National Water-Quality Assessment Project, May 2012 through December 2013\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2016-06-15\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Abstract ...........................................................................................................................................................1 Introduction.....................................................................................................................................................1 Purpose and Scope\\nIntroduction\\nThe equal-area grid method allows for evalu- ation of constituent concentrations at a regional scale (Belitz and others, 2010).\\n8 Groundwater-Quality Data from the National Water-Quality Assessment Project, May 2012 through December 2013\\nATLANTIC OCEAN\\nNORTH CAROLINA\\nVIRGINIA\\nSOUTH CAROLINA\\nRichmond\\n0 50 10 20 30 40 MILES\\n0 10 20 30 40 50 KILOMETERS\\nBase from U.S.\\nThe aquifer system ranks seventh in the Nation as a source of groundwater for public supply and fourth for domestic supply, supplying about 930 million gallons per day pumped for these uses in 2000 (Maupin and Barber, 2005; Maupin and Arnold, 2010; appendix 2).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://bg.copernicus.org/preprints/bg-2017-41/bg-2017-41-SC2-supplement.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Microsoft Word - Reponse_SC1.docx\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"On the other hand, Laloy and Vrugt (2012) demonstrated that DREAM can successfully sample the 25-dimensional, three-modal Gaussian function with the two neighboring modes having a separation of 10 units.\\nLaloy, E., and J.A. Vrugt: High-dimensional posterior exploration of hudrologic models using multiply-try DREAM(zs) and high-performance computing, Water resour. Res., 48, W01526, 2012.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/peterson-tim-j/HydroSight/blob/master/algorithms/calibration/DREAM/DREAM.m\",\n      \"title\": \"HydroSight/algorithms/calibration/DREAM/DREAM.m at master · peterson-tim-j/HydroSight · GitHub\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"%       Environmental Research and Risk Assessment, 23(7), 1011-1026, \\t\\t\\t\\t            %\\n%       doi:10.1007/s00477-008-0274-y, 2009                                                     %\\n%                                                                                               %\\n%   Laloy, E., and J.A.\\nVrugt, High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models      %\\n%       using multiple-try DREAM_(ZS) and high-performance computing, Water Resources Research, %\\n%       48, W01526, doi:10.1029/2011WR010608, 2012. %\\n%                                                                                               %\\n%   Vrugt, J.A., and M.\\nSadegh, Toward diagnostic model calibration and evaluation:             %\\n%       Approximate Bayesian computation, Water Resources Research, 49, 43354345,              %\\n%       doi:10.1002/wrcr.20354, 2013. %\\n%                                                                                               %\\n%   Sadegh, M., and J.A.\\nVrugt, Approximate Bayesian computation using Markov chain Monte       %\\n%       Carlo simulation: DREAM_(ABC), Water Resources Research, doi:10.1002/2014WR015386,      %\\n%       2014. %\\n%                                                                                               %\\n% Version 1.2: August 2010        Generalized likelihood function and prior distribution        %\\n% Version 1.3: September 2010     Explicit treatment of prior distribution                      %\\n% Version 1.4: October 2010       Limits of acceptability (GLUE) and few small changes          %\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2015WR017912\",\n      \"title\": \"A Bayesian approach to improved calibration and prediction of groundwater models with structural error - Xu - 2015 - Water Resources Research - Wiley Online Library\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2015-11-01\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"The presented framework allows explicit treatment of model structural error, while previous applications of Bayesian approaches in the groundwater modeling literature concentrated on parameter uncertainty [ Fienen et al ., 2009 ; Keating et al ., 2010 ; Laloy et al ., 2013 ].\\nIn addition, existing approaches to handling structural error of environmental models [ Kuczera et al ., 2006 ; Lu et al ., 2013 ; Reichert and Schuwirth , 2012 ; Renard et al ., 2010 ; Shi et al ., 2014 ; Schoups and Vrugt , 2010 ] focus on time series data, and mostly rely on relatively simple statistical characterization of model residual\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1029/2009WR008584\",\n      \"title\": \"Optimization and uncertainty assessment of strongly nonlinear ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Optimization and uncertainty assessment of strongly nonlinear ...\\nby EH Keating · 2010 · Cited by 208 — Highly parameterized and CPU-intensive groundwater models are increasingly being used to understand and predict flow and transport through\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=QrvhkvQAAAAJ\",\n      \"title\": \"‪Eric Laloy‬ - ‪Google Scholar‬\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"* High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM (ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nE Laloy, JA Vrugt\\n* Water Resources Research 48 (1) , 2012 | 659 | 2012\\n* Training‐image based geostatistical inversion using a spatial generative adversarial neural network\\nE Laloy, R Hérault, D Jacques, N Linde\\n* Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nE Laloy, B Rogiers, JA Vrugt, D Mallants, D Jacques\\n* Water Resources Research 49 (5), 2664-2682 , 2013 | 313 | 2013\\n* Parameter optimization and uncertainty analysis for plot-scale continuous modeling of runoff using a formal Bayesian approach\\nE Laloy, D Fasbender, CL Bielders\\n* Journal of Hydrology 380 (1-2), 82-93 , 2010 | 68 | 2010\\n* Mass conservative three‐dimensional water tracer distribution from Markov chain Monte Carlo inversion of time‐lapse ground‐penetrating radar data\\nE Laloy, N Linde, JA Vrugt\\n* Water Resources Research 48 (7) , 2012 | 66 | 2012\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.semanticscholar.org/author/E.-Laloy/5346056\",\n      \"title\": \"E. Laloy | Semantic Scholar\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\nE. Laloy J. Vrugt\\nEnvironmental Science, Computer Science\\nHigh‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple‐try DREAM(ZS) and high‐performance computing\\n* 1 January 2012\\nTLDR\\nEfficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nE. Laloy B. Rogiers J. Vrugt D. Mallants D. Jacques\\nEnvironmental Science\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://openalex.org/works/W2133944044\",\n      \"title\": \"Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"description: 2013 article in Water Resources Research by Laloy, Rogiers, Vrugt and 2 others; 264 citations; open access title: Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion image: https://openalex.org/brand-assets/openalex-mark-square.png\\nAuthors: Eric Laloy, Bart Rogiers, Jasper A. Vrugt, Dirk Mallants, Diederik Jacques\\nInstitutions: Belgian Nuclear Research Centre, KU Leuven, University of California, Irvine, University of Amsterdam, Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation, CSIRO Land and Water\\nshow all 6\\nLanguage: English\\nexpansion\\\",\\\"datePublished\\\":\\\"2013-04-03\\\",\\\"inLanguage\\\":\\\"en\\\",\\\"abstract\\\":\\\"Key Points Efficient two‐stage MCMC simulation for CPU‐demanding sampling Real‐world application to the inference of a multi‐layered 3D aquifer model A 2‐5 times observed speed up in sampling efficiency\\\",\\\"author\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Eric\\nLaloy\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5042170410\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4788-3272\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Belgian Nuclear Research\\nCentre\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/institutions/I4210114391\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://ror.org/020xs5r81\\\"],\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"BE\\\"}}]},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Person\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bart\\nRogiers\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5039395337\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8836-0988\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\"