{"type":"text","timestamp":1792455006725,"sessionID":"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M","part":{"id":"prt_156a4bded001CWMqeEeBjUifY8","messageID":"msg_156a4a228001DzUOOZFIOXT3RI","sessionID":"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M","type":"text","text":"I have completed my verification. Here is the final result.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:question\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"We present a new data set of attributes for 671 catchments in the contiguous United States (CONUS) minimally impacted by human activities.\",\n      \"note\": \"Plan research question; needs no source. Its only factual element ('671 CAMELS catchments') matches the CAMELS dataset page (Addor et al. 2017, HESS), so it is corroborated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:hypothesis\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Plan hypothesis/prediction (what the plan predicts); needs no source. The '671 catchments' figure is corroborated by num:camels_n.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:sequential_part\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Plan's sequential-baseline design (4 chains x 100,000 proposal-accept steps), consistent with test_summary's '4 chains x 1e5 iterations'; a design choice, not a factual claim requiring a source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:method\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"\",\n      \"note\": \"Plan method; 2,684 = 671 x 4 chains is internally consistent; needs no source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"card:if_lever\",\n      \"status\": \"SUPPORTED\",\n      \"page_quote\": \"Significant speedups of up to 20 × (CPU) were achieved for calibration, while the scalability analysis indicated 24 × (CPU) and 65 × (GPU) for simulations with larger problem sizes.\",\n      \"note\": \"'>=20x over CPU' is the plan's proxy speedup threshold, corroborated by s_mgb's verified 'up to 20 × 